    "description": "They knew the cost. They signed anyway.\n\nSigned Anyway creates original financial dramas and moral dilemma short films about financial betrayal, financial infidelity, inheritance disputes, corporate ethics, corporate fraud and near-future AI ethics. Each dialogue-driven fictional story reconstructs the evidence behind a hidden financial decision—then asks you to decide who crossed the line.\n\nThe Moral Ledger — every long-form financial and ethical case.\nMoney Between Us — marriage, family and inheritance.\nCorporate Reckonings — boardrooms, fraud and executive choices.\nFuture Verdicts — AI ethics and near-future dilemmas.\nThe Evidence — Shorts that reveal one clue from the full case.\n\nNew 8–11 minute stories; target runtime 9:30.\n\nFictional disclosure: This is an original fictional dramatization created using synthetic performers, voices and environments. No real person, company or event is depicted.",
